I'm dead!

579
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:56,560
Who just outs themselves like that?

580
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:58,160
She's definitely read
a ton of romance novels.

581
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,040
You should be like,

582
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,400
"Babe, this is your invitation card."

583
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,120
"Take it."

584
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:05,840
"If you don't come tomorrow,"

585
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,360
"then we're through from now on."

586
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,040
That's what I'm talking about.

587
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,200
Like those novels.

588
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,510
No, wait.

589
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:19,190
You probably read too many novels.

590
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,080
I had to call it out too.

591
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:24,760
I'm done.

592
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:27,850
This is too funny.

593
00:15:27,870 --> 00:15:29,200
You said you might be pretty sensitive.

594
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:29,550
Why?

595
00:15:29,550 --> 00:15:31,600
What happened,
or what kind of experiences

596
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:33,200
made you this sensitive?

597
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,170
I was born this way.

598
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:35,680
She was born this way. I mean...

599
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:36,720
Honestly,

600
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:37,880
when she said that,

601
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:38,920
my brain kind of short-circuited.

602
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:40,640
What? You don't believe it?

603
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:41,480
No, I was just thinking

604
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:42,840
she probably thought of all kinds

605
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:43,440
of ways to answer,

606
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:44,180
but I didn't expect her

607
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:44,820
to say she was born this way.

608
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:45,760
That totally caught me off guard.

609
00:15:47,590 --> 00:15:49,760
Do you also feel insecure sometimes?

610
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:51,510
I think that goes back to my childhood.

611
00:15:51,510 --> 00:15:52,500
So I don't think

612
00:15:53,050 --> 00:15:54,730
I became this way for no reason.

613
00:15:54,730 --> 00:15:55,610
I can't ask anything of other people,

614
00:15:55,610 --> 00:15:56,480
but I can ask it of myself,

615
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,590
especially when it comes
to my future kids.

616
00:15:58,590 --> 00:15:59,560
You want kids?

617
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:00,020
(Asking)

618
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,120
The things she focuses on...

619
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,920
Her focus is always so unexpected.

620
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,400
She always leaves me speechless
with the things she asks.

621
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:06,800
Whenever she says something,

622
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,440
I just

623
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:08,600
freeze for like three seconds.

624
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,280
You know?

625
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:11,240
I said it was connected to my childhood.

626
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,160
That's why I said I might need

627
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:13,480
to spend more time taking care

628
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:15,880
of my kids in the future.

629
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:16,960
So you want kids?

630
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:17,760
You want kids?

631
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:18,440
You want kids too?

632
00:16:22,030 --> 00:16:22,770
Oh my God.

633
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:24,230
What about you? Do you need glasses?

634
00:16:24,230 --> 00:16:24,860
Are you short-sighted?

635
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:25,960
You forgot again.

636
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:28,070
I did tell you.

637
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,370
Wait.

638
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:34,370
I don't think I got your birthday wrong.

639
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:36,630
What month and day is my birthday?

640
00:16:37,130 --> 00:16:37,850
July.

641
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:38,340
The 16th.

642
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,680
You got it wrong.

643
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:44,480
Oh no.

644
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:45,840
Wait, was that wrong or right?

645
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:46,350
Right.

646
00:16:46,350 --> 00:16:47,010
Right?

647
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:48,670
My birthday is July 16.

648
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:50,520
From now on,
I'll celebrate my birthday on July 16.

649
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,280
I got it wrong.

650
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,280
I wondered what she meant.

651
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,520
Did I remember it wrong?

652
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:55,680
July 17.

653
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:56,240
Yeah.

654
00:16:57,590 --> 00:16:58,140
I got it wrong?

655
00:16:59,450 --> 00:17:00,250
Wrong.

656
00:17:00,990 --> 00:17:01,760
July 17.

657
00:17:03,180 --> 00:17:04,260
(Glares)

658
00:17:04,430 --> 00:17:05,760
Sorry.

659
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,840
You're always apologizing.

660
00:17:08,290 --> 00:17:09,240
Well, I can't just let this slide

661
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:09,800
Yeah.

662
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:10,690
without apologizing.

663
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,760
I can't just let this slide
without apologizing.

664
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:12,840
Yeah, you can't.

665
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,440
You can't remember what she said.

666
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:16,240
I have a bad memory.

667
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:18,490
Why does it

668
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:20,190
feel like you're mad at me?

669
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,310
Don't flatter yourself.

670
00:17:22,550 --> 00:17:23,780
Who's mad at you?

671
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:24,870
You're not mad?

672
00:17:25,570 --> 00:17:27,850
I remember at the dinner,

673
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:29,930
your profile card said
your biggest turn-off

674
00:17:29,930 --> 00:17:32,630
was being unreasonable.

675
00:17:34,370 --> 00:17:35,050
I think sometimes

676
00:17:35,050 --> 00:17:36,080
I can be a little unreasonable.

677
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:37,430
Then go ahead.

678
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:38,640
No.

679
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,480
What?

680
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,320
Your turn-off changes

681
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,560
according to the person?

682
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:43,800
Was I really like that?

683
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:44,840
No way.

684
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:45,600
You were.

685
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,560
I need to record this.

686
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:47,760
I need video proof.

687
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:48,720
"Go ahead".

688
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,240
I was so lovestruck.

689
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:52,040
Watching myself from the outside,

690
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,480
watching my own date is kind of...

691
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:54,760
I'm getting sucked back into it.

692
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:55,390
Oh my God.

693
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,680
Do you think

694
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:00,640
this City Date actually

695
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,000
helped move things forward?

696
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,720
Yeah, definitely.

697
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:04,960
It cleared up the misunderstanding.

698
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:07,680
Things had been awkward for a few days.

699
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,280
At the very least,

700
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:11,080
this helped break the ice.

701
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:13,000
That's pretty important.
Yeah.

702
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:14,800
Sha Yue'er is happy again.

703
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:17,240
Were you happy the day before yesterday?

704
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:19,740
No.

705
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:20,160
I was...

706
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,360
Yeah, I really wasn't happy.

707
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,270
That's all.

708
00:18:22,270 --> 00:18:23,350
Don't be unhappy.

709
00:18:23,830 --> 00:18:25,420
You should enjoy life.

710
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:26,500
Anyone can say that.

711
00:18:27,010 --> 00:18:28,280
But can you actually do it?

712
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:28,650
You...

713
00:18:28,650 --> 00:18:29,470
I can't.

714
00:18:29,470 --> 00:18:31,550
Aren't you more mature than me?

715
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:33,970
So I think...

716
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,360
What's with this chat?

717
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:36,520
You should be able to do it.

718
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:38,000
Don't use that cutesy voice, Sha Yue'er.

719
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:38,840
Give it a rest.

720
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,760
What?

721
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,080
In a minute, you'll be...

722
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:44,810
Oh my God.

723
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,900
If we're all upset,

724
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,320
I feel like you'd put everyone else first.

725
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:52,400
- who counts as "everyone" to you?
- If you had to take care of someone,

726
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:53,190
who would you choose?

727
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,020
(Asks)

728
00:18:55,490 --> 00:18:56,790
If you and everyone else were all upset,

729
00:18:56,790 --> 00:18:58,910
what if I was upset too?

730
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:02,200
I'm not choosing anyone.

731
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,400
I can't answer that.

732
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:06,840
We're talking about a situation

733
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:08,500
where you're fine,

734
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,320
but everyone else and I are upset.

735
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,430
Who would you prioritize?

736
00:19:11,430 --> 00:19:12,390
You.

737
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:12,840
She really

738
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,240
pushed him for an answer.

739
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,160
No.

740
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:16,880
I'd think about you.

741
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:18,080
Thinking.

742
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,160
I think

743
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:20,880
the only way you and everyone else

744
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:21,920
would all be upset

745
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:23,160
is if I secretly

746
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,320
stole everyone's
Master Kong Jasmine coins.

747
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,680
Then I'd be the only one feeling good,

748
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:26,600
while all of you were upset.

749
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,240
That's the only scenario I can think of.

750
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,360
What kind of question is this?

751
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:30,560
Seriously,
what kind of question is that?

752
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,600
Maybe you gave all your Master Kong
Jasmine coins to other people,

753
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:33,680
and that upset her too.

754
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,920
Yeah, I gave

755
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,160
all my Master Kong Jasmine
coins to other people.

756
00:19:37,630 --> 00:19:38,490
Yeah, I've figured you out.

757
00:19:38,490 --> 00:19:39,330
Whenever you ask me something,

758
00:19:39,330 --> 00:19:39,740
Whenever you ask,

759
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:40,060
I'll just tell you straight.

760
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:41,600
Because that's the only answer
you want to hear.

761
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:44,260
You don't even want to hear the process.

762
00:19:44,690 --> 00:19:45,170
You just want to know

763
00:19:45,170 --> 00:19:46,170
if I'd put you first.

764
00:19:46,170 --> 00:19:47,420
And if I say yes,

765
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:47,740
And then...

766
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:49,040
But you can't lie to me.

767
00:19:49,210 --> 00:19:50,140
If you lie to me,

768
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:50,930
then you're a...

769
00:19:52,930 --> 00:19:53,460
A what?

770
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,000
Look, your face is pink
from getting mad.

771
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,200
You're all red.

772
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,800
It's not just your ears anymore.

773
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:00,040
You're mad as a bull now.

774
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,640
You're using the light to hide

775
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:03,920
how red your face has gotten.

776
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:06,640
You really know
how to find the right angle.

777
00:20:07,420 --> 00:20:07,840
Oh my God.

778
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:09,200
You look thinner.
You got mad so hard you lost weight.

779
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:10,320
You've turned me into a pine cone.

780
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:11,800
This...

781
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:12,790
Sha Yue'er.

782
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:14,770
Right?

783
00:20:15,180 --> 00:20:16,120
I've already used my real name.

784
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:17,560
I've used my real name.

785
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:18,980
(Chen Hewen sent a Signal message)
What do you mean?

786
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:21,130
Is using your real name that hard,
Chen Hewen?

787
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:22,120
What do you mean by real name?

788
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:22,920
It means you can

789
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,240
let them know who you
sent your message to.

790
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:25,360
I did.

791
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,080
You can sign your name.

792
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,080
Yeah.

793
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:30,000
I wrote "I'm HW".

794
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:30,890
I see.

795
00:20:31,710 --> 00:20:33,680
The brave get to enjoy life first.

796
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:34,720
Did you enjoy it?

797
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:35,220
I did.

798
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:36,020
I definitely did today.

799
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:41,280
I haven't even used my coins.

800
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,120
Oh my God.

801
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:43,880
(Use them)
Sha Yue'er.

802
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,660
(On who?)
Stop it.

803
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:46,780
(Teasing)

804
00:20:47,550 --> 00:20:48,370
Figure it out yourself.

805
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:49,720
You've left me speechless.

806
00:20:51,510 --> 00:20:52,820
I think it's good for everyone
to get to know you...

807
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:54,780
(Pauses)
"Everyone".

808
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:55,640
No.

809
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,200
Wrong choice of words, Chen Hewen.

810
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,480
He took that back real quick.

811
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:58,960
He paused.

812
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:01,050
To know more about your life

813
00:21:01,050 --> 00:21:01,710
would be nice too.

814
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:03,990
I've actually always had

815
00:21:03,990 --> 00:21:05,280
a lot of wild ideas.

816
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:07,060
Like jumping into the Liangma
River for a swim.

817
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:08,280
Yeah, every time we talk about this,

818
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:08,840
I keep thinking,

819
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:09,800
how does your mind

820
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:11,540
jump from one thing to another so fast?

821
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:12,480
One second you're talking
about having kids,

822
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,840
the next you want to jump
into the Liangma River

823
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:15,040
and go swimming.

824
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:17,930
Then it's settled.

825
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:18,980
Wanna come with me?

826
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:19,800
She invited me.

827
00:21:21,220 --> 00:21:22,050
Oh my God.

828
00:21:24,450 --> 00:21:24,800
Oh my God.

829
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,240
How can you...

830
00:21:26,750 --> 00:21:29,420
Fine, I'll plan a city date.

831
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:31,760
I'll invite you to go swimming
in the Liangma River.

832
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:32,780
(Glances)

833
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:33,480
Other than you two,

834
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,880
no one else would want to go.

835
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:38,110
Of course. Listen, Sha Yue'er,

836
00:21:38,110 --> 00:21:40,220
if you're brave enough to jump in...

837
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:42,000
I swear I'll jump in too.

838
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:48,460
(If you jump, I'll jump too)

839
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:52,080
Perfect.

840
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:53,380
If you chicken out,

841
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:54,190
I'll kick you right in.

842
00:21:54,420 --> 00:21:55,760
I said I'm going in.

843
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:58,240
Why am I like this?

844
00:21:59,990 --> 00:22:01,260
Do you feel like

845
00:22:01,260 --> 00:22:02,190
I'm pretty different

846
00:22:02,190 --> 00:22:03,280
from the person you first met?

847
00:22:03,510 --> 00:22:04,970
I want to know the real you.

848
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:07,620
Now that's good communication.

849
00:22:07,620 --> 00:22:09,940
(I want to know the real you)

850
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:11,720
You really knew what to say back then.

851
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:13,760
That was a good answer.

852
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:14,880
You handled that really well.

853
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:16,280
Your future self must be proud.

854
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:19,440
Now you're proud of yourself.

855
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:20,560
When I first met her,

856
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:21,600
I obviously didn't know

857
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:22,560
what mattered to her.

858
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:23,600
She's quite sensitive

859
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:25,480
and needs constant reassurance.

860
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:26,560
Yeah, I didn't know any of that

861
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:27,280
when we first met.

862
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:28,680
When I first met her,

863
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:29,640
I thought she was pretty talkative.

864
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,760
She was also very open

865
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:31,360
when she greeted everyone.

866
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:32,160
That's why at the dinner,

867
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,320
I described her

868
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:34,200
as confident and composed.

869
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:35,560
After she explained herself,

870
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:36,520
I understood where she was coming from.

871
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:37,480
So I told her

872
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:38,480
to take things at her own pace.

873
00:22:38,920 --> 00:22:39,560
She's a lot like me.

874
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:40,720
Sometimes we both overthink things.

875
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,240
But when she gets
caught up in her thoughts,

876
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:43,400
there's always a reason behind it.

877
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,680
I just don't always see it
from my perspective.

878
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:45,800
So I need to get to know her better.

879
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,120
But after watching that part,

880
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:47,880
I feel like

881
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:49,320
they have their own rhythm too.

882
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:50,760
Maybe that's just

883
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:51,680
how you two get along.

884
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:52,240
All that back and forth.

885
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:52,400
Yeah.

886
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:52,880
All that back and forth.

887
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:53,280
And...

888
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:54,360
Going head-to-head.

889
00:22:54,360 --> 00:22:55,640
Bickering and teasing each other.

890
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:56,880
But I think it creates...

891
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:58,040
a different kind of chemistry.

892
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:58,840
A different kind of chemistry.

893
00:22:58,840 --> 00:22:59,640
It's different.

894
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:00,760
The more time I spend with Sha Yue'er,

895
00:23:00,760 --> 00:23:03,040
the more I realize

896
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:03,920
how many sides she has.

897
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,440
Yeah, she's actually pretty relaxed.

898
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,960
She's very laid-back and genuine.

899
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:07,960
The first time I met her

900
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:09,480
was at that dinner.

901
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:11,640
My first impression was that she
was this cool, aloof beauty.

902
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,400
Yeah.

903
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:14,320
But she was already different

904
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:16,920
on the first day in the house.

905
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:18,440
Then you two became roommates,

906
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:20,520
and every day we'd hear you both
laughing away in the next room.

907
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:21,880
Meanwhile, Si and I

908
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:22,600
were so quiet on our side.

909
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:22,960
You know?

910
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:26,280
What do you think?

911
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,760
What do I think?

912
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:31,560
Now you're suddenly asking me.

913
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:32,840
I haven't spoken in two hours.

914
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:33,360
I...

915
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,680
I have to answer too?

916
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:36,880
So you really came here to watch this.

917
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:39,800
It's also my first time seeing him

918
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:41,560
talk to a girl like this.

919
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,240
Watching his date with Sha Yue'er,

920
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:46,200
it feels like whatever question
Sha Yue'er throws at him,

921
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,800
Chen Hewen can always handle it.

922
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:48,280
I mean,

923
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:49,920
he even handled the question
about having kids.

924
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:55,000
I think you...

925
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,480
you knew

926
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:57,840
how to handle those questions.

927
00:23:57,840 --> 00:23:58,720
Yeah.

928
00:23:58,720 --> 00:23:59,640
High EQ.

929
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,840
You couldn't handle it.

930
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:02,360
Me?

931
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:04,680
I...

932
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:07,280
Maybe it's just

933
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:09,560
because I haven't been
in that situation.

934
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:10,400
I'm not at the having-kids stage yet.

935
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:11,520
So I don't think about that stuff yet.

936
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,440
I can't really relate.

937
00:24:18,230 --> 00:24:19,660
We'll handle the rest.

938
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:21,160
Why are they doing the dishes again?

939
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:22,930
(Thank you)
They've already finished eating again.

940
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,800
Were only the four of us eating?

941
00:24:27,520 --> 00:24:29,040
They got straight to eating.

942
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:30,770
I forgot to eat.

943
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:32,910
So you skipped breakfast today?

944
00:24:33,670 --> 00:24:34,860
Lately, when I wake up,

945
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:36,050
I feel like I've...

946
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:37,880
Stay back, Cui Kaiyi.

947
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:38,840
(Tilts head)

948
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:40,040
What are you doing?

949
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:41,520
That was too sweet.

950
00:24:41,520 --> 00:24:43,120
Why didn't you look at me back then?

951
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:45,600
I should be... Wait, I didn't?

952
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:46,900
aged 20 years overnight.

953
00:24:49,520 --> 00:24:50,600
I was too shy to look.

954
00:24:51,360 --> 00:24:52,440
You were that shy?

955
00:24:52,920 --> 00:24:55,640
The dishes looked better than me?

956
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:56,880
Cui Kaiyi was probably thinking,
look at me.

957
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:58,160
Look at me.

958
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:59,240
I didn't dare look.

959
00:24:59,240 --> 00:24:59,600
I couldn't.

960
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:00,440
Didn't dare to look.

961
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:01,800
I really couldn't.

962
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:02,680
Before,

963
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:03,720
when you weren't

964
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:04,640
that close,

965
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:05,680
he'd keep looking at you.

966
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:06,840
But now that you're
standing next to him,

967
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:07,840
he won't even look at you.

968
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:14,340
Careful, that breaks really easily.

969
00:25:14,340 --> 00:25:15,440
Why did you give him this?

970
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:17,200
Because he...

971
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:18,360
(Is this for him?)
he needed something comforting.

972
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:19,560
Comforting? Why?

973
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:21,600
He said he likes being outdoors

974
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:22,240
and getting fresh air.

975
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:24,320
But he's in the house every day,

976
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:26,600
so I thought I'd give him a little plant
to take care of.

977
00:25:27,630 --> 00:25:28,980
This a gift for you.

978
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:30,610
(This is something I gave him)
This is so pretty.

979
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:31,290
A potted plant.

980
00:25:31,290 --> 00:25:34,300
It's a terrarium.

981
00:25:36,670 --> 00:25:39,080
Is it for fish?

982
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:40,720
For keeping fish?

983
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:43,280
I thought you had to fill it with water.

984
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:44,960
Like those...

985
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:45,840
I thought they came over

986
00:25:45,840 --> 00:25:46,760
to see what was going on.

987
00:25:46,760 --> 00:25:48,320
(I even looked through it)
What's this for?

988
00:25:48,320 --> 00:25:49,720
What do you mean?

989
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:50,600
It's Tianjin dialect.

990
00:25:50,600 --> 00:25:51,760
Say something in Tianjin dialect.

991
00:25:53,320 --> 00:25:54,960
Ma just means what.

992
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:55,600
That's what it means.

993
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:56,340
What's it for?

994
00:25:56,340 --> 00:25:56,960
It means what are you selling?

995
00:25:56,960 --> 00:25:57,760
That's what it means.

996
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:58,200
Yeah.

997
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:58,560
What?

998
00:25:58,560 --> 00:25:59,320
What's this?

999
00:26:01,320 --> 00:26:02,120
That startled me.

1000
00:26:09,960 --> 00:26:11,840
A musical genius
and his talented partner.

1001
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:13,920
Thanks.

1002
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:15,440
Love this.

1003
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:17,680
We've got front-row seats.

1004
00:26:17,910 --> 00:26:19,930
Is this the Signal House March?

1005
00:26:20,060 --> 00:26:21,720
(Impressive)
The Signal House March.

1006
00:26:21,720 --> 00:26:22,840
The Signal House March.

1007
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:25,040
I've never heard a guitar and flute
duet before.

1008
00:26:25,040 --> 00:26:25,800
Me neither.

1009
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:26,400
Same.

1010
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:27,200
Who would've thought?

1011
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:28,080
We were both shocked.

1012
00:26:28,080 --> 00:26:29,160
Seriously.

1013
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:30,080
Anything can work together.

1014
00:26:30,080 --> 00:26:30,640
Here we go.

1015
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:31,680
The sound really carries.

1016
00:26:31,680 --> 00:26:32,020
Yeah.

1017
00:26:32,020 --> 00:26:32,640
You can hear it throughout
the whole house.

1018
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:33,760
The flute is really loud.

1019
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:34,240
It's so bright.

1020
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,490
(Get ready to enjoy)
Yeah, really bright.

1021
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:36,200
It sounds great.

1022
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:37,260
Can you play that one?

1023
00:26:37,870 --> 00:26:38,410
Which one?

1024
00:26:38,410 --> 00:26:41,010
The one from "The Legend
of the White Snake".

1025
00:26:41,280 --> 00:26:42,170
What's it called again?

1026
00:26:42,170 --> 00:26:43,290
I forgot too.

1027
00:26:43,290 --> 00:26:44,300
Hum it, and I can play it.

1028
00:26:44,300 --> 00:26:45,990
♪Bai Suzhen from Qingcheng Mountain♪

1029
00:26:45,990 --> 00:26:46,800
This one?

1030
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:47,790
Yeah.

1031
00:26:49,260 --> 00:26:52,500
(Plays it with ease)

1032
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:57,420
Oh my God.

1033
00:26:57,850 --> 00:26:59,280
You need to stand up, you know?

1034
00:26:59,280 --> 00:27:00,280
You have to play it standing up.

1035
00:27:00,300 --> 00:27:01,160
Play it standing up.

1036
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:02,280
Oh my God.

1037
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:02,800
Like this.

1038
00:27:02,810 --> 00:27:03,550
You know...

1039
00:27:03,550 --> 00:27:04,940
Then you'll tip over in seconds.

1040
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:06,360
(Walks off on his own)
I'm dying.

1041
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:07,120
I'll row beside you.

1042
00:27:08,450 --> 00:27:09,290
Sing a couple of lines.

1043
00:27:09,550 --> 00:27:10,930
I'll be your backup.

1044
00:27:12,900 --> 00:27:15,840
♪Time keeps rushing by♪

1045
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:16,750
♪You're all I care about♪

1046
00:27:16,750 --> 00:27:17,560
Oh my God.

1047
00:27:17,760 --> 00:27:18,640
They're actually playing together.

1048
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,000
They're actually playing together.

1049
00:27:21,280 --> 00:27:22,040
Wait.

1050
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:22,760
What's going on here?

1051
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:28,080
People really don't share
the same joys and sorrows.

1052
00:27:28,080 --> 00:27:28,640
Not at all.

1053
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:30,120
It's all sweetness down here,

1054
00:27:30,120 --> 00:27:31,720
and misery upstairs.

1055
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:33,480
The four of us are terrible.

1056
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:34,560
How could we do that?

1057
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:35,560
Seriously.

1058
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:38,310
Oh my God.

1059
00:27:39,280 --> 00:27:40,200
Sun Bohan's writing a letter.

1060
00:27:40,560 --> 00:27:41,440
Seriously.

1061
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:42,920
It feels like this music

1062
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:43,560
fits everyone somehow.

1063
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,480
It works with every scene,

1064
00:27:44,480 --> 00:27:45,320
just in a different way.

1065
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:47,400
And then there's Zhao Xilun,
feeling down all by himself.

1066
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:49,440
No wonder there were
so few people in the lounge that day.

1067
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:50,280
Oh my God.

1068
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,560
Fang, was that your first time

1069
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:55,360
hearing Yu Yang play the flute?

1070
00:27:55,360 --> 00:27:56,360
Yeah, and I'd actually

1071
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:58,880
been looking forward to it for days.

1072
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:00,200
He kept hinting at it,

1073
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:02,280
saying he used to play the flute.

1074
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:04,240
I kept asking when

1075
00:28:04,240 --> 00:28:05,000
I'd get to hear him play.

1076
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:05,960
Then that day,

1077
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:07,120
he happened to bring it to the house.

1078
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:08,280
And somehow,

1079
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:09,880
it worked perfectly with the guitar.

1080
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:11,360
And so I could play the guitar,

1081
00:28:11,360 --> 00:28:12,520
I even had my nails removed

1082
00:28:12,520 --> 00:28:13,840
a few days before.

1083
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:16,160
You were both preparing for this.

1084
00:28:16,160 --> 00:28:16,840
Perfect.

1085
00:28:16,840 --> 00:28:17,880
All for this one performance.

1086
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:18,680
So charming.

1087
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:21,720
I just feel

1088
00:28:21,720 --> 00:28:22,440
like...

1089
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:24,760
when I saw him in his element,

1090
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:25,800
he really knew what he was doing.

1091
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:27,880
Whenever he's doing something
he's really good at,

1092
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:28,360
I just feel like

1093
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:29,840
he shines.

1094
00:28:29,840 --> 00:28:30,680
He really shines.

1095
00:28:36,180 --> 00:28:38,220
(Changes Fang's bandage)

1096
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:39,240
Time for your medicine, right?

1097
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:39,440
Yeah.

1098
00:28:39,440 --> 00:28:40,400
Yu Yang always changes Fang's...

1099
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:41,120
Bandage.

1100
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:42,000
Every night.

1101
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,500
He applies the medicine and wraps it up.

1102
00:28:43,500 --> 00:28:44,530
(Thanks, Chen Hewen)
It's become a daily routine.

1103
00:28:44,530 --> 00:28:45,050
Thanks.

1104
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:48,440
Everyone's eating.

1105
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,480
And everyone's watching the drama.

1106
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:51,200
Too bad I wasn't there.

1107
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:53,840
Weren't we in the study?

1108
00:28:53,860 --> 00:28:54,680
(Where were you?)
Yeah.

1109
00:28:55,550 --> 00:28:56,560
Playing badminton.

1110
00:28:57,800 --> 00:28:58,970
A badminton date.

1111
00:28:59,210 --> 00:28:59,740
Seriously?

1112
00:29:02,940 --> 00:29:03,620
Chen Hewen.

1113
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:04,360
Wait.

1114
00:29:05,950 --> 00:29:07,260
Now you're in your element.

1115
00:29:07,390 --> 00:29:08,530
(In his element)
Not really.

1116
00:29:08,530 --> 00:29:09,060
I was just messing around.

1117
00:29:09,060 --> 00:29:09,800
Here comes his moment.

1118
00:29:12,020 --> 00:29:13,900
(Looks back and forth)

1119
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:16,560
He's blinking again.

1120
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:19,920
Keep blinking and you'll fall asleep.

1121
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:23,440
What's bothering you, Zhao Xilun?

1122
00:29:24,520 --> 00:29:25,720
Tell us. Don't hold it in.

1123
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:27,840
Why do you keep closing your eyes
and shutting down?

1124
00:29:28,440 --> 00:29:29,800
It feels like being squeezed.

1125
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:31,160
It's basically...

1126
00:29:31,160 --> 00:29:32,520
Trapped by this massage chair.

1127
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:34,760
Getting completely squished.

1128
00:29:41,760 --> 00:29:43,400
This looks like a senior center.

1129
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,200
Massage chairs,

1130
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:47,960
leg massagers.

1131
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:49,480
Foot care,

1132
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:50,200
snacks.

1133
00:29:51,120 --> 00:29:53,000
Why does everyone
seem so old this episode?

1134
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:54,840
Everyone aged thirty years.

1135
00:29:55,520 --> 00:29:57,320
Everyone has their own story.

1136
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:00,120
Drinking water to avoid the awkwardness.

1137
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:02,000
How long are you gonna drink?

1138
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:02,600
Until I finish it.

1139
00:30:16,040 --> 00:30:16,900
(Backs away)
What's that about?

1140
00:30:20,750 --> 00:30:21,550
Hi.

1141
00:30:24,720 --> 00:30:25,830
Want one?

1142
00:30:25,830 --> 00:30:26,450
What's this?

1143
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:27,860
Throat lozenges.

1144
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:28,790
My throat's been bothering me, remember?

1145
00:30:29,190 --> 00:30:29,920
Oh, right.

1146
00:30:30,320 --> 00:30:30,920
Want another one?

1147
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:36,840
Wait, the moment you left, he came out.

1148
00:30:37,510 --> 00:30:38,490
This is...

1149
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:40,260
the photo Meng took of you

1150
00:30:40,260 --> 00:30:41,160
the other day.

1151
00:30:41,700 --> 00:30:42,600
A photo of me?

1152
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:44,640
I have something else for you too.

1153
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:48,400
Perfect timing.

1154
00:30:50,120 --> 00:30:50,960
They can really edit this.

1155
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:52,040
Oh my God!

1156
00:30:52,040 --> 00:30:53,440
This is so dramatic.

1157
00:30:53,440 --> 00:30:54,560
This...

1158
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:55,080
This is wild.

1159
00:30:55,080 --> 00:30:56,120
The timing

1160
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:56,760
is insane.

1161
00:30:56,760 --> 00:30:57,960
You didn't know, did you?

1162
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:58,880
I had no idea.

1163
00:30:58,880 --> 00:30:59,520
I've only seen

1164
00:30:59,520 --> 00:31:00,440
scenes like this in movies.

1165
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:01,360
One comes, the other goes.

1166
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:03,520
Even Sha Yue'er was stunned.

1167
00:31:03,520 --> 00:31:05,200
One leaves, and another shows up.

1168
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:06,160
Oh my God.

1169
00:31:06,840 --> 00:31:07,680
That's it?

1170
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:09,160
That's it.

1171
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:10,400
Seriously, that was amazing!

1172
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:12,200
Can the four of us come back
next episode?

1173
00:31:12,200 --> 00:31:13,320
Please, I'm begging you.

1174
00:31:13,320 --> 00:31:14,520
I still want to watch more.

1175
00:31:14,520 --> 00:31:15,600
The other three don't have to come.

1176
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:16,600
I just need to be here.

1177
00:31:16,600 --> 00:31:18,120
Or bring all eight of us next time.

1178
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:19,360
The four of us can stand in the back

1179
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:20,800
and keep watching from there.

1180
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:21,520
I'll squeeze in anywhere.

1181
00:31:21,520 --> 00:31:22,960
I'll even sit on the floor.

1182
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:24,400
We can give the seated guests

1183
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:25,680
back massages or something.

1184
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:26,840
We're happy to help out.

1185
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:28,320
Don't stop here. I can't take it.

1186
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:31,140
This is killing me. Oh my God.

1187
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:33,000
Let's take a photo together

1188
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:33,680
to remember this.

1189
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:34,960
- We can put all our photos
- Sure.

1190
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,040
up there, right?

1191
00:31:36,040 --> 00:31:36,400
Okay.

1192
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:37,720
Come on, let's take a photo.

1193
00:31:38,620 --> 00:31:39,080
I'll count to three.

1194
00:31:39,080 --> 00:31:39,480
What was it again?

1195
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:40,100
What was it, guys?

1196
00:31:40,100 --> 00:31:40,820
Watching Heart Signal with You,

1197
00:31:40,820 --> 00:31:41,280
the sparks never end.

1198
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:41,840
See you next time.

1199
00:31:42,520 --> 00:31:43,640
You're a pro at this now.

1200
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:45,160
No wonder. You've done this three times.

1201
00:31:45,160 --> 00:31:45,920
Come on, let's say the slogan.

1202
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:47,040
Three, two, one.

1203
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:48,600
Watching Heart Signal with You,

1204
00:31:48,600 --> 00:31:49,960
the sparks never end.

1205
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:51,560
See you next time.

1206
00:31:53,640 --> 00:31:54,600
Let's see which one looks better.

1207
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:56,040
Which of these two?

1208
00:31:56,040 --> 00:31:56,440
What do you think?

1209
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:57,320
Let's compare them.

1210
00:31:57,720 --> 00:31:59,000
I think this one.

1211
00:31:59,000 --> 00:31:59,480
This one looks better.

1212
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:00,480
I think it'd look great right here.

1213
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:01,360
Sure, let's put it up.

1214
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:04,560
Looks good.

1215
00:32:04,560 --> 00:32:05,280
Okay.

1216
00:32:07,660 --> 00:32:09,380
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

1217
00:32:09,380 --> 00:32:11,060
(New episodes every Mon and Tue at noon)

1218
